risk, landing points that are close to obstacles will be penalized to bring the final landing point
away from obstacles as much as possible.
Criteria 3 considers distance from the takeoff point. Landing point accuracy becomes harder
to predict as the hop distance increases. To reach landing points as accurately as possible, it is
important to prioritize closer jumps. Hence, points that are farther away will be penalized.
Criteria 4 considers the proximity of the landing point to edges of the surface. Due to
instability, it is important to leave room for error. Prioritizing points that are closer to the center
will reduce the risk of hopping past edges past which the terrain is unknown.
